Smart Tree (st): a fast, context-aware directory visualizer — a modern `tree`
built for humans and AI agents. This rustybox `extras` applet delegates to the
standalone smart-tree binary (github.com/8b-is/smart-tree); every argument is
passed straight through.

	st                 visualize the current directory
	st PATH -d 5       a path, to depth 5
	st --mode ai       token-compact output for AI/agent context

Requires the `st` binary on PATH (cargo install smart-tree), or set $RUSTYBOX_ST
to point at it. This applet execs that binary rather than linking it, to keep
the rustybox core small and audited.
